 ## Overview
-WildGS-SLAM is a robust monocular RGB 3D Gaussian Splatting SLAM system designed for dynamic "in-the-wild" scenes [S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of tracking and mapping failure caused by dynamic distractors (moving objects/people) by making the optimization residual uncertainty-aware [S1]. Unlike standard Gaussian SLAM methods that treat all pixels as static map constraints, WildGS-SLAM uses a learned uncertainty map to weight photometric and geometric errors, effectively suppressing unreliable observations from moving objects during bundle adjustment [S1].
+WildGS-SLAM is a robust monocular RGB 3D Gaussian Splatting SLAM system designed for dynamic "in-the-wild" scenes [S2, unofficial]. It addresses the failure mode of dynamic distractors by making the optimization residual uncertainty-aware, weighting photometric and geometric errors based on predicted uncertainty to suppress unreliable observations [S1]. Unlike standard Gaussian SLAM methods that treat all pixels as equally valid map constraints, WildGS-SLAM dynamically identifies and ignores moving objects, reconstructing a clean static Gaussian map [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
